          "why_it_matters": "This is more than a SistaStrings stop in Washington. The Library is putting the duo on its Stradivari instruments for the world premiere of Mayari, a McKim Fund commission by Larissa Maestro, placing their Black-church-rooted, classically trained string language inside a new-work tradition that the Library has sustained for generations. The rare instruments are part of the musical proposition, not decoration: the point is to hear a living cross-genre duo encounter a piece written for this institutional context while the work is still entering the world.",
